Well, I was hoping to get myself a birdie but now this year's
tournament is over...
It was an ambitious goal, given that before the tournament I'd ascended
K,S (in last year's tourney) and W, once each. In between the many YASD
and YAVSDs this year, I managed to ascend a male Orcish barbarian.
Genoless, artifact wishless, Elberethless and with no serious polying
(some link to a cheat sheet saying what eg conduct 0xc00 means might
help, google found me the details on Aardvark Jo's patch from last
year's discussion though). I don't rember too clearly what happened.
Cleaver, then Stormy with a side order of Frostbrand. GDSM and AoR.
Kill, kill, kill. The only *really* exciting moment was heading up
Rodney's tower. Hello purple L. Oh, you've brought Yeenoghu (I think).
Goodbye Lich. Yeenoghu's taking some time to keel over. Oh, he wants
some more friends along at the party. What's that D. And so, for the
first time in my nethack experience, I come face to face with
Demogorgan. I slow down. Now dealing with two major demons at once
isn't a good idea, so I leave Yeenoghu behind and take the stairs back
to the main dungeon with Demogorgan at my heels. I control teleport to
the up staircase and start hitting him. You're sick. Thwack. You're
sicker. Full healing. Thwack. You're sick again. Thwack. Demogorgan
dies. I drink another full healing. (The plan if not the exact number
of thwacks is right). I get a couple more potions out of the bag, and a
cup of tea from the kitchen, and dispatch Yeenoghu. Offering many
prayers of thanks to Arioch (and silently to Set) I head back to up the
tower. The rest is not too hard. WoD deals with Rodney. The Sanctum
falls slowly (I was trying the Stealth graveyard technique, but my
tactics still need (more than a little) work. No major scares on the
planes. I take on and take out Pestilance, wrong altar. Not having run
out of WoD charges I take him out again, then Famine. Right altar. You
ascend to demigodhood. And that's my first Barbarian ascended.
After that I kill off many lawful dwarven Arcs, lawful dwarven Valks
and neutral Gnomic Wizards. (I was trying for the Birdie and dreaming
of three alignments). I nearly got one of my wizards there. She had a
nice start and when she felt up to taking on dragons, reverse genocided
silvers and made her own armour. Haste self substituted for speed
boots, and on clearing out the Castle, she decided to try for wishless,
genoless, polyless. I hadn't got a perfect AK, but it looked good
enough, though another magic marker would have been really nice. All
goes relatively smoothly until I get the Amulet, which puts a damper on
my ability to kill things (Magicbane not really cutting it (sorry) and
having to be careful about mana again). Care and attention take her up
to the planes, which cause few problems until Astral. Then I started
making mistakes. I forgot to take off the Levitation boots, which nixed
jumping (spell only). I didn't realise my mistake until I got to the
place I needed to jump (as I was saving my magic for charm and magic
missiles). And then my second mistake. Before I hit astral, I should
have sorted my inventory to have all of my c. 10 full healing in the
main inventory. And probably the Castle wand, though it would have hurt
to break wishless at that late stage. My wizard slogged her way left to
the first altar, burning WoTele and WoDeath charges on the way. Wrong
altar, so back past Famine and head for Pestilance in the centre. Wrong
altar. Thank you for showing me the error of my ways oh mighty RNG.
Right past Death it is then. (I didn't have a Helmet of Opposite
Alignment, and probably wouldn't have used it even if I had). I try to
jump past Death so I can whistle in my menagarie to slow him down. You
flail around. As changing footware with Death taking 30HP a turn off me
seemed unwise, I dodged past Death. Ouch, that hurt. There's just this
door, a small room and I'm there. Priests and Angels blocking the way,
and Death at my heels. Last WoD charge. And the remenants are still
blocking the doorway. Death is right behind me. Last WoTele charge and
there's still someone in the way. I hit them. Drink the last full
healing in my main inventory (there's still half a dozen in the BOH).
Now there's a couple of priests, angels and a huge pile of insects in
the way. I struggle on for a turn or two more but to no avail DYWYPI?
Killed by Death on the astral plane (with the amulet). At least it
wasn't a giant beatle that administered the coups de grace.
After that the only other close attempt was another Wizard on the last
day of the tournament (I'd had a week when I'd unexpectedly had to
travel so no Nethack). Going strong, but suffered greatly from being
started at about 6pm UK time. With such distractions as dinner, it was
2.30 am when she vapourised her SDSM, but studded leather and a AoR
should have seen her through to a replacement. By 3.00am, she's got
mapping, L15 and has reached Medusa (but not done the quest, meaning to
wish up an AK with the Castle wand first). I'm tired, but I'm not
getting any less tired before the tournament finishes so, having
Levitation boots, I start across the water. I'm careful with the eels,
and am heading onwards when I notice I'm Weak. I wonder when that
happened? I know, I'll just kill these Chickatrices and then I'll
eat... And I think the rest writes itself.
Anyhow, thanks for the tornament and next year, I'll try to do better.

